WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.540
The first time CBS News came on was September the second, 1963.

2
00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:10.100
And what’s so relevant about that is if you Google the inaugural edition,

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:17.760
as they’re . . . he [Walter Cronkite] starts the CBS Evening News (which is the number one news now) in Nantucket,

4
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:21.800
Massachusetts, talking to then-president John Kennedy.

5
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:23.820
Then he breaks the interview.

6
00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:27.540
At that time, he breaks back to Iberville Parish.

7
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:35.140
There’s a bunch of blacks who are in a church listening to a black civil rights guy.

8
00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:40.100
Well, inside that church was my mom with a little kid three months old—myself.

9
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:45.400
The whites roll into that church and they wanted to get Spivey Gordon, who’s the speaker.

10
00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.540
I think his name was Spivey Gordon [James Farmer].

11
00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:52.700
They rode in, they beat the blacks with cattle prongs and et cetera.

12
00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:57.760
My uncle was in there, Clarence Hill, who’s my grandfather’s name—he’s named after.

13
00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.440
Beat the living daylights out of him.

14
00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:03.600
And CBS Evening News broke to that story.

15
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:06.940
Why it’s important, ultimately, they tried to get the speaker.

16
00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:17.860
And the black leadership back then took him and brought him to the local funeral home and put him in a hearse.

17
00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:21.630
Put him in a casket and drove him the only way out of Plaquemine, Louisiana.

18
00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:22.440
To Baton Rouge.

19
00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:27.080
And put him on a Greyhound bus and sent him back to Atlanta.

20
00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:30.360
The issue was they were looking house to house, looking for him to hang him.

21
00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:34.760
Because they didn’t want blacks having these civil rights folks there.

22
00:01:34.760 --> 00:01:39.660
The dumbness of the whites were they were checking every car, but when that hearse passed by,

23
00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:46.360
they took their hats off on their horses and let that hearse pass through, and unbeknownst to them, this man was in that car.

24
00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:47.700
In that hearse, and he got away.
